; `%(expr)` in an automated posting's account is expanded before any
; `$name`.  A template with no `$name` of its own keeps its `%(expr)`
; output as written, as v3.4.1 did (P:).  In a template that has both,
; a `$name` in the `%(expr)` output is replaced like one written in
; the template (M:).

= /^Expenses:Food/
    (P:%(payee))                   1
    (M:%(payee):$account_base)     1

2024/01/03 Deli $account_base
    Expenses:Food:Dining    $1.00
    Assets:Cash

test bal --flat
              $-1.00  Assets:Cash
               $1.00  Expenses:Food:Dining
               $1.00  M:Deli Dining:Dining
               $1.00  P:Deli $account_base
--------------------
               $2.00
end test
